## ABSTRACT
Heterogeneousmaterials madeofmetal-organicframeworks(MOFs)andopticallactive nanomaterialshaveatracted intensive interests inrecentyearsduetotheirdistinctphysicochemicalproperties,butcontrolablefabricationofthesematerialsremains challenging yet.In this work,we report anew strategyto in situ fabricateheterogeneous nanomaterials basedon $\mathsf{U i O-}66\mathsf{-N H}_{2}$ and upconversionnanorods (UCNRs)viaahierarchicalanddynamicassembly process.Core-satellte structured UiO-66- $N H_{2}@$ UCNRs havebeen successfullfabricated,andtheformation mechanismwasthoroughly investigated bythecombined useof scanning electron microscopy (SEM)and Fouriertransform infrared (FTIR)spectroscopy.Our resultsrevealed the involvement of three main stages: supramolecular assembly of ${\mathsf{U i O}}{-}66{-}{\mathsf{N H}}_{2}$ precursors with UCNRs, nucleation and growth of ${\mathsf{U i O}}{\mathsf{-}}66{\mathsf{-}}{\mathsf{N H}}_{2}$ crystal, and dynamic assembly with UCNRs accompanied by Ostwald ripening. Furthermore, based on the hereditaryopticaland porousfeatures of theheterogeneousnanomaterials,anenhancedmultimodalsynergistic anticancer platformhas been established by integrating near-infrared (NIRtriggered photodynamictherapy (PDT)and pH-triggered anticancerdrugdelivery,asconfimed bycelularexperiments.Thepresent study providesanewavenue fordeveloping advanced functional heterogeneous nanomaterials via the hierarchical and dynamic assembly strategy.
